  "term": "criminal intent",
  "definition": "Criminal intent is the underlying intention behind a criminal act. In behavior analysis, it is treated as a shared factor across traditional and cyber crimes and may be inferred from patterns in a suspect’s behavior, including behavior reflected in digital evidence.",
